#4471 is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. The reports say otherwise. Each report is
placed by its tenant (locale, booking form) and channel, not by its subject line or intake's tag.

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. "Wrong day on the
invite" fits all three problems, so all three landed in #4471. Intake's `intakeTag` comes from the
browser, not the tenant, and disagrees with the tenant-based cause for many reports.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not fix the booking-v3 form hint or the one-day move. Each has its own
ticket in the repo that holds this page.
</Callout>

## What to do

- `parser`: read dates in the tenant's locale. This is the fix already queued.
- `hint`: make booking-v3's hint match how the form reads the date.
- `one-day-move`: look at time zones and DST when the invite is written; the reports name clients in
  different zones getting different days.

